```
Z(N,m)>=2 binom(r,2)^m/r!,
Z_0/Z <= min(1, m! binom(binom(N,2),m/2) r!
                 /[2 binom(r,2)^m]).                    (9)
```

Choose `r=floor(m/log m)` for large `N`. For the stated power regimes,
this lies between two and `N`. Elementary factorial/binomial bounds give

```
log(Z_0/Z)
