+
+Coordinator checked primary DYZ Prop.1 eq.(13), normalization pages 4-5,
+and primary Vakil conventions/Cor.1.5/Prop.3.2. The existing positive count
+code matched independent labeled-permutation DP in 91 cells N<=6,m<=12.
+Direct word/macro/per-word-probability tests passed all required cases,
+including N4,m8 with 131040 connected and 140160 total words.
+global_mass_results.json stores 369 exact g<=1 coverage certificates through
+N64,m128. At m=2N, coverage equals 80/81 at N3, 4375/4672 at N4,
+approximately .026822 at N16 and 3.9064e-6 at N32.
+
+global_consequence.md contains a new provisional proof: at m=2N the
+restricted set has all labels active and all components genus one; its
+global mass tends to zero using a factorial upper bound and an embedded
+subgroup return lower bound. This is a method limitation, not hardness.
+
+Next actions: finish candidate exact checks, preserve a frozen candidate
+version, obtain referee audit only after its blind report is saved; request
+nonauthor review of global consequence. Keep all rejected versions/witnesses.
