+# Checkpoint — candidate recursion and global certificate
+
+Updated 2026-09-07 approximately 21:19 UTC; initial checkpoint was saved
+within the first 20 minutes. Run active; target T0 provisional, not accepted.
+Native session ID:
+01a07db2-4703-7312-ae54-75fcdc0bdc13.
+
+Cap read on entry; activation 21:07:10 UTC, wrapup 00:37:10 UTC on Sep 8,
+hard deadline 01:07:10 UTC. No clock reset or new process/service launched.
+One native goal was created without a token budget.
+
+The three required workers are dispatched in fresh contexts as
+/root/r1_recursive, /root/r2_structural, /root/r3_referee, all explicitly
+gpt-6-astra/ultra. The referee has only the separate blind input. Each owns
+its assigned role directory and must preserve exact assignment/report inputs.
+
+Read AGENTS, GOAL_SPEC standards, HANDOFF context/rank section, project skill
+and experiment references, audit skill/protocol/probability regressions,
+September 5 phase diagram/ledger/coordinator and component report, and M97.
+Prior accepted claims are dependencies, not external certifications. The
+newer September 5 coverage conflicts with the dense-only HANDOFF summary;
+this is recorded in run_manifest.md rather than silently editing a theorem.
+
+Major result: r1 supplied a complete provisional exact sampler proof
+R1-T1 at roles/r1-recursive/proof.md. The last-transposition decomposition
+closes on arbitrary connected endpoints of genera 0/1. The exponential
+cycle-subset sum is replaced by a positive DP on total size, cycle count,
+and marked count using Vakil's positive genus-one formula. Coordinator read
+the full proof; executable validation and a nonauthor audit are still required.
+No theorem is promoted. r2 independently found the genus-zero endpoint
+primitive and is developing a unicyclic cut-object sampler. Referee blind
+work remains isolated until its report is frozen.
+
+Coordinator checked primary DYZ Prop.1 eq.(13), normalization pages 4-5,
+and primary Vakil conventions/Cor.1.5/Prop.3.2. The existing positive count
+code matched independent labeled-permutation DP in 91 cells N<=6,m<=12.
+Direct word/macro/per-word-probability tests passed all required cases,
+including N4,m8 with 131040 connected and 140160 total words.
+global_mass_results.json stores 369 exact g<=1 coverage certificates through
+N64,m128. At m=2N, coverage equals 80/81 at N3, 4375/4672 at N4,
+approximately .026822 at N16 and 3.9064e-6 at N32.
+
+global_consequence.md contains a new provisional proof: at m=2N the
+restricted set has all labels active and all components genus one; its
+global mass tends to zero using a factorial upper bound and an embedded
+subgroup return lower bound. This is a method limitation, not hardness.
+
+Next actions: finish candidate exact checks, preserve a frozen candidate
+version, obtain referee audit only after its blind report is saved; request
+nonauthor review of global consequence. Keep all rejected versions/witnesses.
