experiments/20260907-genus-one-sampler/proof.md:136:For any fixed parent word with a disconnected final-letter branch, multiply: selected branch mass D/C_parent; exact assignment mass W/D; child masses 1/C_A and 1/C_B; interleaving mass 1/binom(L,r_A). By (2) this equals 1/C_parent. For a connected branch it is (C_child/C_parent)(1/C_child)=1/C_parent. The disjoint reconstruction proves this is the full word probability, with no omitted preimages or extra multiplicity. Induction proves exact uniformity and exact support, product and length. This is an exact conditional-probability identity, not a product of unconditional accuracy estimates.
experiments/20260907-genus-one-sampler/proof.md:142:The DP coefficients sum at most 2^N allocations, each with at most 2^N marked subsets, products bounded by N^N, and marked sums <=N; hence have O(N log(N+1)) bits. Formula powers have exponent at most N and the only negative exponents are >=-2 on each component size (>=-1 in the genus-one factor). The product of the (a_i-1)! denominators divides N!. Every rational summand's denominator therefore divides 24(N!)^5, a uniform integer of O(N log(N+1)) bits. All terms are nonnegative, their magnitudes and sums are at most exp(O(N log(N+1))), and reduced rational intermediates consequently have O(N log(N+1)) bits. The completed branch counts are integers bounded by binom(N,2)^(2N), with the same bit bound. Standard exact arithmetic therefore gives a polynomial bit bound; allowing O(B^3) bit operations for a reduced-rational operation on B-bit operands gives the conservative O(N^10 log^3(N+1)) bound, plus polynomial expected fair-bit work. The theorem only needs an expected polynomial bound; no dependence on b is necessary for the exact sampler.
experiments/20260907-genus-one-sampler/proof.md:146:Load-bearing external dependency: the specified Vakil count formulas and their fixed-permutation normalization. Everything after R1-C1 is elementary combinatorial disintegration and dynamic programming. Exact executable validation of R1-C4/C5 passed as recorded in report.md and results.json. The current first remaining certification step is fresh audit; these are supplied as complete candidate arguments, not presumed accepted. If the audit accepts them, no mathematical completion oracle remains missing for g<=1. This does not give a general arbitrary-genus sampler, a prescribed exposed-prefix connectivity oracle, all-length global sampling, a local-chain gap, or polynomial complexity in log N wires.

